    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7366": {
      "title": "Club Sports Head Men's Wrestling Coach",
      "description": "Club Sports Head Men's Wrestling Coach | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Club Sports Head Men's Wrestling Coach Req #908 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Monday, September 14, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S . , Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; School of Computer Science & Engineering and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, R.N., & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change—in their own lives, professions and in their communities. The Princeton Review includes SHU in its Best 391 Colleges: 2026 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2025 Edition . Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; a Division I athletics program and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary The Head Men's Wrestling Coach is responsible for recruiting and retaining players, planning and conducting practices, coaching during matches, and managing other administrative responsibilities associated with the team. This part-time position runs from September 1st to May 15th each academic year. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Responsible for the recruitment of prospective students who meet university admission standards. Responsible for all league-required paperwork, as well as understanding all associated rules. Responsible for retention of team members, particularly first-year students, and ensuring their transition into college is seamless. Work with club sports staff to develop a cohesive program and highlight those via social media and the Club Media website. Develop a recruitment Plan beyond the upcoming season. Communicate and collaborate with the department regarding practice and match times/dates. Prepare, plan, and coordinate practice schedules each week and provide proper and high-quality instruction to student-athletes to ensure all team members are prepared for competition. Coordinate with the Athletic Training staff regarding player safety and medical needs. Oversee all game day operations including game planning, transportation, and game roster, in conjunction with other coaching staff. Work closely with the Associate Director for Club Sports & Intramurals on the preparation of the season, schedule, and recruitment. Responsible for ongoing recruitment and retention of student-athletes. Manage coaching staff and student manager staff as hired by the Club Sports department. Foster strong, professional relationships with league representatives and officials, consistently demonstrating positive sportsmanship and conduct that reflects the University’s mission and values. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes A bachelor’s degree is preferred. 1-3 years of coaching experience at the high school, prep, junior, or collegiate level Must be willing and available to work nights and weekends, as the majority of games are Friday-Sunday Possess experience working with diverse staff, including college-age students Must maintain coaching certification or have the ability to acquire certification CPR/First Aid Certification Unusual Working Conditions Potential late nights due to practices and weekend availability for matches or competitions. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow us to share information with third party advertising and analytics partners and use your information for advertising and analytics purposes. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
