    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7222": {
      "title": "Athletics - Assistant or Associate Athletic Director, Business Operations & SWA",
      "description": "Athletics - Assistant  or Associate Athletic Director, Business Operations & SWA | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Athletics - Assistant  or Associate Athletic Director, Business Operations & SWA Req #893 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Monday, September 7, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S . , Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; School of Computer Science & Engineering and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, R.N., & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change—in their own lives, professions and in their communities. The Princeton Review includes SHU in its Best 391 Colleges: 2026 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2025 Edition . Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; a Division I athletics program and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. This position will be filled at either the Assistant or Associate level, based on the successful candidate's qualifications and experience. Position Summary The Assistant or Associate Athletic Director, Business Operations provides strategic and operational leadership for the business functions of the Department of Athletics. The position oversees financial management, budgeting, purchasing, contracts, revenue and expense tracking, and business processes to ensure fiscal responsibility, compliance, and efficient departmental operations. Primary Responsibilities & Duties Manage all day to day business paperwork including, but not limited to, expense vouchers, Concur reports, purchase orders, journal entries, and budget transfers for Athletics Interface with accounts payable, purchasing, and payroll departments to facilitate processing, including budget inquiry research as necessary Meet with coaches to review budget reports and prepare forecasts Plan, prepare, and reconcile all cash advances for meals, recruiting, and travel Audit Concur reports for accuracy and completeness, performing reclasses as needed Provide monthly Concur report updates to full department Complete the Metro Survey, AHA survey, CAA survey, and assist with the Equity in Athletics Disclosure Act and NCAA audit Prepare monthly team, administrative and fundraising reports for athletics Set up all new vendors on Unimarket Sign off on transactions in Unimarket at level zero, checking for proper accounting and workflow Assist Senior Associate Athletics Director and Executive Director of Athletics with zero-based budgeting annually Responsible for deposit processing Prepare ad hoc financial reports and analysis on request Become a resource for coaching and administrative staff on business functions, policies and procedures Serve as sport administrator for several assigned sports Serve as Senior Woman Administrator, attending league meetings as required Stay up to date on the college athletics landscape to be able to contribute to strategic discussions at conference level Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Attributes Bachelor’s degree required; a degree in Accounting, Finance or Sport Management is preferred Experience with budgeting for Division I Intercollegiate Athletics preferred or experience in a University business office Ability to work independently and as part of a team Effective organizational and time management skills Detail oriented and able to maintain confidentiality Unusual Working Conditions The employee is required to work evenings and weekends, as needed. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow us to share information with third party advertising and analytics partners and use your information for advertising and analytics purposes. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7487": {
      "title": "Graduate Admissions - Associate Director of Graduate Admissions & Recruitment",
      "description": "Graduate Admissions - Associate Director of Graduate Admissions & Recruitment | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Graduate Admissions - Associate Director of Graduate Admissions & Recruitment Req #803 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, September 24, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Monday, September 28, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary Contribute to the achievement of new graduate student recruitment goals, including the dual degree and combined degree. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Meet and exceed targets for new dual degree and combined degree students and new external students in assigned markets. Achieve benchmarks for conversion rates throughout the recruitment funnel and work to continually improve conversation at all stages—inquiry, applicant, deposit, enrolled. Assist in the development and enhancement of the recruitment plan for dual and combined degree students and recruitment plans for assigned programs. Work with graduate program directors, undergraduate faculty and department chairs, and academic advisement and academic operations in the recruitment and retention of dual degree and combined degree students. Work with Director of Admissions and Recruitment to identify new sources of prospective students. Develop and maintain productive relationships with graduate program directors in assigned programs. Collaborate with the Office of Undergraduate Admissions on the effective recruitment of dual degree students. Deliver an excellent customer service experience for all prospective students, managing coordinated, proactive follow up with each candidate throughout the funnel.  Cultivate relationships with each candidate to address their unique graduate enrollment process. Advise and counsel students on program benefits, application processes and requirements. Represent the University and individual graduate programs at off campus recruitment events, college fairs and other programs to increase program visibility and generate inquiries. Plan present at, and participate in on-campus and virtual recruitment programs and events, including events in conjunction with undergraduate admissions, undergraduate academic clubs and organizations, Career Center events, and graduate program events. Develop and utilize deep knowledge of all assigned graduate programs to effectively communicate program distinctions and experiences to candidates. Develop deep knowledge of all aspects of the University, including student support services, to assist in effective recruitment. Develop and maintain expertise in Slate functionality. Develop and maintain current knowledge of competitors for each assigned program. Maintain current knowledge of external factors impacting enrollment trends for each graduate program. Contribute to a positive, collaborative, results-focused culture and environment as part of the Graduate Admissions team. Develop and engage with professional networks online (e.g., LinkedIn) to support the achievement of enrollment goals. Attend divisional and university meetings and gatherings; Participate and be visible in the University community, in particular attending programs within the colleges relating to assigned graduate programs and supporting the activities and achievements of graduate students. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Master’s degree preferred. Minimum of one to three years of successful admissions and recruitment experience. Experience with graduate student populations preferred. Strong self-starter who can work well independently and as part of a team. Outstanding public speaking ability, writing skills and interpersonal skills. Experience using a sales or admissions CRM. Slate experience preferred. Strong customer service orientation and excellent relationship-building skills. Desire to work flexible hours at time to be responsive to adult students and working professionals. Valid driver’s license with clean motor vehicle record is required. Unusual Working Conditions Full time work schedule; Some evening hours required to engage with/outreach to prospective students, participate in recruitment events, and meet deadlines. Some weekend hours are required for recruitment events and activities. Some travel required. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Enrollment Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Travel Required Yes Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
