    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7471": {
      "title": "Athletics - Assistant Director of Athletic Communications",
      "description": "Athletics - Assistant Director of Athletic Communications | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Athletics - Assistant Director of Athletic Communications Req #919 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, September 24, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary Assist in covering all Sacred Heart's varsity sports and will be the primary contact for selected sports, including men’s basketball. The assistant director will serve as the liaison between the media, student-athletes and coaches. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Serve as the primary athletic communications for assigned athletic programs including men’s basketball. Coordinate all aspects of publicity efforts for assigned sports, including but not limited to - in-game and historical statistics, preparation and dissemination of information to the media and promotion of student-athletes and coaches to media and for postseason and weekly awards. Work closely with production staff on ESPN+ and other broadcasts, assist in production of content for YouTube, social media and in-game video board content. Maintain the athletic website with pre- and post-game stories, stats, records, etc. Assist in maintaining areas of the website not directly associated with teams, i.e. Staff Directory, Compliance Pages, Academic Pages, etc. Assist in the hiring and management of work study student assistants and interns. Participate in creation and implementation of department social media strategy and campaigns to increase publicity and event attendance. Serve as key strategist and producer for the creation of engaging content to promote events, accolades, awards and recognition of Sacred Heart Athletics. Provide support as member of stat crews, public address announcer, etc. Help maintain historical records and archives to produce content on alumni and past teams. Serve as a key member of Athletics Department Communications and Marketing team that makes decisions shaping the department’s communication. Assist in providing creative direction within the Communications and Marketing team, facilitating a cohesive execution of creative materials, including in the creation of the Annual Report. Supervise Communications Game Day Staff. Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor’s degree and/or equivalent, in communications, journalism, sports management or a related field of study. 4- 5 years of experience in a college or professional athletic setting as graduate assistant, full-time intern or full-time. Candidates should have strong oral and writing skills, proficiency in desktop publishing (Adobe InDesign, Photoshop, etc.), experience with in-game statistical software (Genius & StatCrew) new media applications (Instagram Twitter, etc) and basic computer applications. Advanced proficiency in writing and interviewing with knowledge of the Adobe Creative Suite, specifically Premiere Pro and Photoshop. Advanced proficiency in use and knowledge of all social media platforms, specifically Facebook, Instagram, and Twitter. Proficient knowledge of graphics, photography, video editing. Must possess a valid state-issued driver’s license with a clean driving record. Unusual Working Conditions Full-time position.  Nights, weekends, and some travel required. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
