    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7505": {
      "title": "Computer Science - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Computer Science - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Computer Science - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Req #921 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Sunday, September 27, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University (SHU), located in Fairfield, Connecticut, houses its School of Computing & Engineering (SCE) within the College of Arts & Sciences . SCE offers two graduate programs (M.S. in Computer Science & Information Technology and M.S. in Cybersecurity), and seven undergraduate Bachelor of Science programs—Computer Science, Information Technology, Game Design & Development, Cybersecurity, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, and Mechanical Engineering. To support the continued growth of its computing programs, the School of Computing and Engineering invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor for the ABET-accredited B.S. in Computer Science program at SHU. The successful candidate will be a dynamic and innovative educator-scholar committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching, student mentoring, and scholarly activity. The position emphasizes hands-on, project-based learning and active engagement with students, while contributing to curriculum development and continuous program improvement aligned with ABET accreditation standards. The anticipated start date for this position is August 2027 (Fall semester). Primary responsibilities include: Designing and teaching problem-based, hands-on undergraduate courses in computer science, with an emphasis on machine learning, generative AI, natural language processing, and computer vision . Conducting scholarly computer science and artificial intelligence research appropriate for a teaching-focused institution. Supervising graduate and undergraduate student research as well as mentoring senior capstone design projects. Collaborating with industry partners and the SHU community on interdisciplinary projects. Supporting continuous program improvement and ABET accreditation activities. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence or a closely related discipline, completed by the start date of the appointment. Expertise in artificial intelligence, machine learning and language models preferred. Commitment to a highly interactive, student-centered learning environment Openness to innovative and hands-on pedagogical approaches Demonstrated potential for scholarly research and professional growth Experience developing or maintaining industry collaborations Preferred Qualifications: Experience with active or project-based learning approaches Experience applying machine learning techniques within any scientific context Evidence of an ongoing scholarly research agenda and publication activity Experience developing or maintaining industry collaborations To apply, please submit the following materials: A cover letter describing your interest in the position and how your background aligns with the responsibilities and qualifications A curriculum vitae A statement of teaching philosophy A statement describing past and future research interests Contact information for three professional references (letters of recommendation will be required from final candidates) Review of applications will begin December 1st, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date for the position is August 2027 (Fall semester). Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Samah Senbel, at senbels@sacredheart.edu Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Doctorate Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7493": {
      "title": "Sociology, Criminology, & Criminal Justice - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Sociology, Criminology, & Criminal Justice - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Sociology, Criminology, & Criminal Justice - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Req #923 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Sunday, September 27, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here The Department of Sociology, Criminology & Criminal Justice in the College of Arts & Sciences at Sacred Heart University invites applications for an on-ground Tenure-Track Assistant Professor position to begin in August 2027. We seek a colleague committed to excellent undergraduate teaching and an active scholarly agenda. Generalists are welcome, and we encourage applicants from all areas of criminology and criminal justice to apply. We are particularly interested in candidates who can teach core courses in the criminal justice major such as introduction to corrections, along with introduction to criminal justice, research methods, as well as courses that support our criminology minor. The Department of Sociology, Criminology, and Criminal Justice at Sacred Heart University brings together faculty who study crime, justice, and social inequality from sociological and criminological perspectives. Our undergraduate programs combine rigorous theoretical grounding with applied learning, preparing students for careers in the justice system, human services, and public policy, as well as for graduate and professional study. Faculty are active scholars who mentor students closely, and our students benefit from small classes, research opportunities, and internship experiences. The department is growing and, in the Spring of 2028, we will launch a new Master of Arts in Criminology & Criminal Justice (MCCJ) . The program will prepare students for advanced roles in the justice system and related fields and provide a foundation for doctoral study. Our forthcoming MCCJ program reflects the department's commitment to evidence-based practice, social justice, and community engagement. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to teach and mentor graduate students. Responsibilities: The successful candidate will: Teach core courses required of the criminal justice major, including Introduction to Corrections, along with Introduction to Criminal Justice, Research Methods, and courses that support our Criminology minor. Develop and teach upper-level electives that reflect their expertise and complement existing departmental offerings Advise and mentor undergraduate students, including in research and internship experiences Maintain an active program of scholarship, including peer-reviewed publication Contribute to departmental, college, and university service Requirements: A Ph.D. in Criminology or Criminal Justice. A J.D. alone will not satisfy the degree requirement. Candidates who are ABD will be considered, though a Ph.D. must be in-hand by the start date. Demonstrated potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching Evidence of scholarly productivity or clear promise of it Ability to teach across the Criminology and Criminal Justice curriculum Application Instructions: Qualified candidates are invited to submit: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy A research statement contact information for three references (letters of recommendation will be required from final candidates) Graduate transcripts. Copies of transcripts are acceptable during the initial stage; however official transcripts will be required upon a formal offer of employment. Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Please direct any questions to the Department Chair, Dr. Bethany Van Brown at vanbrownb@sacredheart.edu Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Doctorate Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8071": {
      "title": "Notre Dame Prep - Assistant Director of Advancement",
      "description": "Notre Dame Prep - Assistant Director of Advancement | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Notre Dame Prep - Assistant Director of Advancement Req #817 220 Jefferson St, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Friday, October 30, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a cover letter, resume, or curriculum vitae, along with the contact information for three letters of reference, who will be contacted only if you are selected for an interview. Only applications submitted via our Career portal will be considered. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary The Assistant Director of Advancement supports the Director of Advancement in executing the school’s fundraising and donor engagement efforts. This role focuses on annual and restricted giving campaigns, special events, donor stewardship, alumni relations programming, and prospect pipeline development. As a member of a small department, this role serves as a key partner in the execution of the school’s advancement program. Primary focus areas: Manage the implementation of the NDP Fund (Annual Fund) and other annual fundraising initiatives Assist in donor cultivation, stewardship, and communications Maintain accurate donor records and advancement systems Help expand participation across parents, alumni, and the broader school community Principal Duties & Responsibilities Annual Fund & Campaign Support Plan and execute annual fundraising drives; e.g., NDP Fund and various restricted campaigns, mailings, digital campaigns, phone-a-thons, and participation drives Support class-based fundraising initiatives and senior giving programs Track and report on annual unrestricted and restricted giving progress and participation Donor Relations & Stewardship Assist with donor cultivation and stewardship activities, including correspondence and recognition Help coordinate donor meetings, events, and follow-up communications Support donor research and prospect identification Database & Gift Processing Provide timely, accurate constituent recording in the donor database (Little Green Light/Razor’s Edge/ CRM) Produce reports and analytics to support decision-making Events & Engagement Coordinate major school fundraisers including, but not limited to, the Gala, Golf Tournament, and Walk-a-thon Work collaboratively with the Advancement team to advance alumni engagement opportunities, including planning reunions Assist in coordinating logistics and donor engagement opportunities Recruit, train, and support volunteers involved in fundraising initiatives Serve as the department’s liaison with the Notre Dame Parent Association’s leadership team. Communications Support development of fundraising materials, newsletters, and digital outreach Assist in maintaining consistent messaging across advancement communications Grants & Administrative Support Assist in grant research and preparation of proposals and reports Provide administrative support for advancement initiatives and campaigns Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Attributes Bachelor’s degree required 3–5 years of experience in development, nonprofit work, or related field preferred Strong interpersonal, analytical and organizational skills; sharp attention to detail Commitment to maintaining confidentiality Detail-oriented with ability to manage multiple projects Experience with databases or CRM systems preferred Commitment to the mission of Catholic education Unusual Working Conditions Ability to work evenings or weekends as needed. Evening activities are scheduled in advance. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits: The maximum annual salary for this position is $85,000. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Travel Required No Scan this QR code and apply! Download 220 Jefferson St, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
