    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8063": {
      "title": "Great River Golf Club - Greens & Grounds Technician",
      "description": "Great River Golf Club - Greens & Grounds Technician | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Great River Golf Club - Greens & Grounds Technician Req #890 130 Coram Ln, Milford, CT 06461, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Thursday, October 15, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary Responsible for maintaining the facilities and grounds at Great River Golf Club. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Perform preventative maintenance of facilities and buildings. Perform routine maintenance tasks such as mowing, trimming, and edging to keep the golf course and surrounding areas neat and well-groomed. Maintain golf course features, including tees, greens, fairways, roughs, bunkers, cart paths, and parking lot areas to ensure they meet established standards. Perform duties utilizing rakes, shovels, brooms, and various hand tools. Participate in irrigation activities, including watering, repairing, and adjusting sprinkler systems as needed. Perform special tasks related to drainage, tree maintenance, and course construction and shaping. Engage in landscaping tasks such as planting, pruning, weeding, mulching, and filling divots to enhance the course's natural beauty. Assist with golf course renovation projects, including aerating, seeding, and sodding. Monitor the course for any signs of damage or wear and promptly report issues to the supervisor. Operate and maintain various groundskeeping equipment, such as walk-behind mowers, blowers, backpack blowers, and string trimmers, ensuring tools are clean, safe, and in good working order. Operate and maintain heavy equipment, such as backhoes, skid steers, Ventrac Tractors, and tractors, as directed. Operate a golf cart. Provide exceptional customer service by interacting professionally with members and guests and addressing any concerns or questions related to the course conditions. Perform other duties as assigned by the Golf Course Superintendent or management. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Attributes There are no formal education requirements; a high school diploma or equivalent is preferred. A valid driver’s license with no current violations is required. Knowledge of golf rules and golf course etiquette is preferred. Previous experience in landscaping, golf course groundskeeping, or related fields is preferred. Demonstrated ability to operate groundskeeping equipment safely, including lawnmowers, trimmers, and blowers. Demonstrated ability to operate heavy equipment safely, including backhoes, skid steers, Ventrac tractors, and tractors. Strong attention to detail and commitment to maintaining high course appearance and functionality standards. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Must be able to perform manual labor tasks, including lifting up to 50 pounds, carrying, pushing, pulling, bending, stooping, stretching, twisting, reaching with arms and/or legs, and walking extensively throughout the day. Willingness and ability to work in various outdoor environmental and weather conditions, including exposure to insects, pests, and varying temperatures. Ability to understand and communicate written and verbal instructions accurately. Must be dependable and punctual; arrive on time and prepared to start working. Unusual Working Conditions Availability to work early mornings, weekends, and holidays as required by the golf course schedule. Duties require physical strength, standing, and endurance in various weather conditions for extended periods outdoors. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. In accordance with Connecticut General Statutes § 31-51v, applicants selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment drug test as a condition of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of both the background check and drug test. Compensation & Benefits : The hourly compensation for this position ranges from $20.00 to $25.00. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Facilities Pay Type Hourly Scan this QR code and apply! Download 130 Coram Ln, Milford, CT 06461, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8054": {
      "title": "Career Development - Director of Career & Professional Development, CAS",
      "description": "Career Development - Director of Career & Professional Development, CAS | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Career Development - Director of Career & Professional Development, CAS Req #892 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Monday, October 5, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary Oversee all career development functions for the College of Arts & Sciences. Oversee student programming, event planning, and internal marketing related to internship and employment planning for the college. Collaborate with other directors to manage external relations, employer development, and on-campus recruiting for the office. Provide career planning and job search counseling to all students and alumni in assigned majors. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Provide comprehensive career coaching to CAS students in skills such as self-exploration, branding, networking, resumes, cover letter creation, LinkedIn, interview preparation, career selection, internship and full-time employment, and job offer negotiations. Maintain consistent communication with employer partners and proactively identify internship and full-time employment opportunities. Source and identify prospective employer partners and manage relationship development. Proactively outreach to faculty and key administrators to increase collaboration with faculty in assigned College/majors and to support the career development needs of their students. Identify and secure employer partners for participation in on-campus events. Oversee the marketing of CAS services to employers, students, and the University community. Plan, implement, and oversee office events and student programs including career fairs, etiquette dinners, employer information sessions, career panels, and on-campus interviews. Assist with the gathering of internship and outcomes data for CAS and for internal and external publications. Develop and maintain an external presence with local employer partners. Administer workshops, seminars, and class presentations related to student and faculty needs. Utilize Career Management Platform software to facilitate career development activities and communications. Support Associate Directors and other Directors in execution of signature office programs/events. Contribute to management of the departmental website as needed. Liaise with Alumni and leverage relationships related to existing students' career planning and placement. Attend University-wide functions or events, at the discretion of the Executive Director of Career Development. Assist with departmental Strategic Planning and other collaboration with the Senior Director and CAS Dean. Complete special projects as requested. Participate and be visible in the University community, supporting the activities and achievements of students and alumni. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree in related field preferred. 3-5 years of experience in higher education in the career development function. Prefer candidates with experience providing job search counseling to undergraduate students. Proficiency in all Microsoft Office applications and the Internet. Willingness and ability to learn new software including the office’s career management system. Excellent oral and written communication skills Comfort speaking to groups Strong customer service orientation Energetic and able to think out of the box Interest in working directly with students in a student services capacity Strong knowledge of and interest in the field of career development and job market trends Unusual Working Conditions Some evening and weekend hours are required. Travel may be required for events and professional development opportunities Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The maximum salary range for this position is $77,160 Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Student Support Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Travel Required Yes Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
