    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8027": {
      "title": "Information Technology",
      "description": "Information Technology - Systems Analyst, Finance | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Information Technology - Systems Analyst, Finance Req #918 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary Provide system administration, support, and systems analysis of assigned applications. Provide level 2 software application support for the university user community. Resource for level 1 system analyst to ensure timely resolution of tickets. This is a 100% on-campus position. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Monitor, maintain, and coordinate minor upgrades for technology systems in assigned responsibility areas, including problem-solving and implementing system modifications. Coordinate the execution of user acceptance testing procedures and develop test cases to serve the overall quality assurance process. Analyze business process issues and/or problems and provide consulting assistance to system users; conduct research on possible solutions and make recommendations based on findings; suggest, design, test, implement, and evaluate solutions. Brainstorm new ways to add more functionality to systems Coordinate creation, updates, and retirement of interfaces for supported applications Demonstrate thorough and friendly customer service to the university community Communicate clearly and professionally, both verbally and in writing, to different audiences May perform all or some of the responsibilities above and other related duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor’s Degree in a computer-related or business-related discipline required Minimum 2 years experience in system administration, level 2 application support, and troubleshooting Experience with and understanding of academic environment and familiarity with academic-related applications preferred Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, as well as strong interpersonal skills Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail Possess a strong work ethic and team player mentality Ability to take initiative and be self-motivated, as well as collaborate successfully with a team Familiarity with Ellucian Colleague Systems Experience with Financial Applications Ability to work on campus full-time Unusual Working Conditions Working after hours, on weekends, and holidays to complete assigned tasks is sometimes required. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $65,460 - 72,420 Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Information Technology Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8013": {
      "title": "Athletics - Assistant Director of Athletic Communications",
      "description": "Athletics - Assistant Director of Athletic Communications | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Athletics - Assistant Director of Athletic Communications Req #919 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary Assist in covering all of Sacred Heart's varsity sports and serve as the primary contact for selected sports, including men’s basketball. The assistant director will serve as the liaison among the media, student-athletes, and coaches. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Serve as the primary athletic communications for assigned athletic programs including men’s basketball. Coordinate all aspects of publicity efforts for assigned sports, including but not limited to - in-game and historical statistics, preparation and dissemination of information to the media and promotion of student-athletes and coaches to media and for postseason and weekly awards. Work closely with production staff on ESPN+ and other broadcasts, assist in production of content for YouTube, social media and in-game video board content. Maintain the athletic website with pre- and post-game stories, stats, records, etc. Assist in maintaining areas of the website not directly associated with teams, i.e. Staff Directory, Compliance Pages, Academic Pages, etc. Assist in the hiring and management of work study student assistants and interns. Participate in creation and implementation of department social media strategy and campaigns to increase publicity and event attendance. Serve as key strategist and producer for the creation of engaging content to promote events, accolades, awards and recognition of Sacred Heart Athletics. Provide support as member of stat crews, public address announcer, etc. Help maintain historical records and archives to produce content on alumni and past teams. Serve as a key member of Athletics Department Communications and Marketing team that makes decisions shaping the department’s communication. Assist in providing creative direction within the Communications and Marketing team, facilitating a cohesive execution of creative materials, including in the creation of the Annual Report. Supervise Communications Game Day Staff. Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor’s degree and/or equivalent, in communications, journalism, sports management or a related field of study. 4-5 years of experience in a college or professional athletic setting as graduate assistant, full-time intern or full-time. Candidates should have strong oral and writing skills, proficiency in desktop publishing (Adobe InDesign, Photoshop, etc.), experience with in-game statistical software (Genius & StatCrew) new media applications (Instagram Twitter, etc.) and basic computer applications. Advanced proficiency in writing and interviewing with knowledge of the Adobe Creative Suite, specifically Premiere Pro and Photoshop. Advanced proficiency in use and knowledge of all social media platforms, specifically Facebook, Instagram, and Twitter. Proficient knowledge of graphics, photography, video editing. Must possess a valid state-issued driver’s license with a clean driving record. Unusual Working Conditions Full-time position. Nights, weekends, and some travel required. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $47,050 - $58,960 Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8006": {
      "title": "Business Office",
      "description": "Business Office - Accountant II | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Business Office - Accountant II Req #920 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Accountant II supports accounting operations across multiple functional areas by assisting with the accurate recording, reconciliation, analysis, and reporting of financial activity. This role helps ensure the integrity of the general ledger and supports timely and accurate financial reporting in accordance with established policies and procedures. The position requires solid analytical skills to review account activity, evaluate trends and variances, support estimates and accruals, and identify issues requiring further research or resolution. Additionally, the Accountant II assists in monitoring and reporting the University’s actual results, preparing ad hoc financial analysis, and responding to internal and external financial requests. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Account Reconciliations and Analysis: Own assigned balance sheet and general ledger account reconciliations, including cash and cash equivalents, accrued liabilities, allowance for doubtful accounts, and other assigned accounts. Analyze account activity, research reconciling items, identify trends or unusual transactions, and coordinate with internal departments to resolve discrepancies timely and accurately. Journal Entries and Month-End Close Support: Prepare, review, and post routine and recurring journal entries, including accruals, reversals, expense allocations, revenue activity, and other supporting adjustments. Ensure entries are properly supported, accurately classified, and recorded in accordance with accounting policies and month-end close timelines. Variance Analysis and Financial Review: Perform account-level variance analysis to support the accuracy and completeness of financial records. Review fluctuations against expectations, investigate discrepancies, summarize findings, and escalate items requiring further research or corrective action. General Ledger Maintenance and Governance: Support general ledger governance through account setup, chart of accounts maintenance, account review, and validation of appropriate account usage. Assist in maintaining consistent accounting structure and supporting documentation across departments and financial processes. Compliance and Internal Controls: Follow and reinforce established accounting procedures and internal controls to support accurate, complete, and compliant financial reporting. Assist with approval reviews, compliance checks, documentation requests, and process improvements that strengthen accountability and reduce financial risk. Audit and External Reporting Support: Support the annual audit process by preparing schedules, gathering supporting documentation, responding to audit inquiries, and researching assigned items. Assist with external reporting requests and other compliance-related reviews as needed. NCAA and Agreed-Upon Procedures Support: Assist with the annual NCAA agreed-upon procedures process by compiling supporting documentation, reviewing assigned financial activity, responding to requests, and coordinating follow-up items to ensure timely completion Customer Service and Cross-Functional Support: Monitor and respond to inbound requests from University departments related to journal entries, account reconciliations, general ledger activity, and other accounting matters. Partner with internal stakeholders to research issues, provide guidance, and ensure timely and accurate resolution in accordance with Business Office procedures. Additional Responsibilities : Perform other accounting, analysis, reporting, and special project duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Characteristics Bachelor’s degree in Accounting CPA or MBA desired, not required Minimum 2-3 years of related experience. Advanced working knowledge of Excel. Excellent analytical, interpersonal, communication, problem-solving, and organizational skills. Knowledge of accounting software programming desired. Ability to learn new responsibilities, to work independently and as part of a team. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $56,930 - $80,000 Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Finance Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7998": {
      "title": "Facilities & Construction",
      "description": "Facilities & Construction - Electrician Lead | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Facilities & Construction - Electrician Lead Req #925 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Electrician Lead is responsible for installing, maintaining, troubleshooting, repairing, and inspecting electrical systems and equipment throughout the University's campus. This position supports the safe, reliable, and efficient operation of academic, residential, administrative, athletic, and healthcare facilities. The Electrician Lead performs skilled electrical work in accordance with applicable codes, regulations, and University standards while contributing to preventative maintenance programs, emergency response activities, energy conservation initiatives, and continuous operational improvement efforts. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Install, maintain, troubleshoot, and repair electrical systems and equipment including: Power distribution systems Lighting and lighting controls Emergency power systems Motor controls Variable Frequency Drives (VFDs) Transformers Switchgear and panelboards Fire alarm interfaces Electrical components associated with HVAC and mechanical systems Diagnose electrical issues using testing and diagnostic equipment and implement corrective actions. Perform preventive, predictive, and corrective maintenance on electrical systems and equipment. Install new electrical circuits, conduit, wiring, fixtures, outlets, and equipment as required. Inspect campus facilities and equipment to identify deficiencies, safety concerns, and maintenance needs. Read and interpret: Electrical drawings Blueprints One-line diagrams Schematics Specifications Technical manuals Respond to service requests and emergency calls promptly and professionally. Support campus construction, renovation, and capital improvement projects. Maintain compliance with National Electrical Code (NEC), Connecticut State Electrical Code, OSHA regulations, and University standards. Coordinate work activities with Facilities Operations staff, contractors, vendors, and campus stakeholders. Utilize Computerized Maintenance Management Systems (CMMS) to document work, labor, materials, and equipment history. Assist with operating and maintaining emergency generators and associated transfer switch systems. Participate in on-call rotation as required and respond to after-hours emergencies. Support University sustainability and energy conservation initiatives through efficient operation and optimization of electrical systems. Maintain inventory of electrical materials, tools, and supplies. Perform other tasks assigned by the manager to meet the university's needs. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes High school diploma or equivalent required; accredited electrical trade school, vocational program, apprenticeship program, or equivalent technical training preferred. Connecticut E-1 Unlimited Electrical Journeyperson License required. Minimum 5 years of commercial, institutional, healthcare, or higher education electrical experience preferred. Strong knowledge of electrical theory, power distribution systems, motor controls, and electrical safety practices. Thorough understanding of the National Electrical Code (NEC) and applicable state and local codes. Experience working with generators, transfer switches, and uninterruptible power supply (UPS) systems preferred. Knowledge of lockout/tagout procedures and electrical safety standards. Familiarity with Building Management Systems (BMS/BAS) preferred. Proficiency with computers, mobile devices, and work order management systems. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong communication and customer service skills. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment. Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Unusual Working Conditions Exposure to energized electrical equipment and circuits while performing testing, troubleshooting, maintenance, and repair activities. Work may be performed in electrical and mechanical rooms, utility tunnels, crawl spaces, above-ceiling areas, confined spaces, rooftops, and other restricted-access areas. Exposure to varying environmental conditions, including heat, cold, humidity, dust, noise, vibration, and inclement weather. Required use of appropriate Personal Protective Equipment (PPE), including arc-flash protective clothing, insulated gloves, safety glasses, hard hats, hearing protection, and other safety equipment as required. Work may involve climbing ladders, scaffolding, and personnel lifts; working at heights; and working around high-voltage electrical distribution equipment, generators, transformers, switchgear, and transfer switches. Must be able to lift, carry, push, and pull electrical equipment, materials, tools, and supplies weighing up to 50 pounds, with assistance for heavier items. Must be available to respond to electrical and life-safety emergencies and participate in an on-call rotation, which may include evenings, weekends, holidays, planned utility shutdowns, and other work outside normal business hours. Must be able to safely perform work in occupied campus facilities while minimizing disruption to University operations. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. In accordance with Connecticut General Statutes § 31-51v, applicants selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment drug test as a condition of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of both the background check and drug test. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $40.59 - $48.72 per hour Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Facilities Pay Type Hourly Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7979": {
      "title": "Facilities & Construction",
      "description": "Facilities & Construction - Plumber Lead | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Facilities & Construction - Plumber Lead Req #926 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 1, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Plumber Lead is responsible for installing, maintaining, repairing, inspecting, and operating plumbing, piping, drainage, water distribution, sanitary sewer, and related mechanical systems throughout Sacred Heart University's campus. The position ensures that all plumbing systems operate safely, efficiently, and in compliance with applicable local, state, and federal codes while supporting the University's commitment to providing a safe, comfortable, and reliable environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. The Plumber Lead performs preventive and corrective maintenance, responds to emergency service calls, assists with renovation and construction projects, and collaborates with other Facilities personnel to maintain campus infrastructure and support institutional objectives. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Maintains and repairs plumbing systems serving academic buildings, residence halls, athletic facilities, dining facilities, laboratories, administrative offices, and campus support buildings. Responsible for diagnosing and resolving issues involving domestic water, sanitary waste, storm drainage, natural gas piping, pumps, fixtures, valves, water heaters, backflow prevention devices, and related equipment. Performs preventative maintenance inspections to maximize system reliability and reduce operational disruptions. Responds to emergency situations including leaks, pipe failures, sewer backups, water quality concerns, and equipment malfunctions. Supports campus renovation and capital improvement projects by reviewing plans, installing piping systems, coordinating utility shutdowns, and ensuring code compliance. Documents work performed, labor hours, materials used, and equipment history. Works independently with minimal supervision while coordinating with Facilities, Public Safety, contractors, vendors, and project managers. May provide technical guidance and mentoring to maintenance technicians, apprentices, and other Facilities personnel. Participates in an on-call rotation and may be required to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and during campus emergencies. Thorough knowledge of plumbing principles, practices, materials, methods, and tools. Comprehensive understanding of Connecticut State Plumbing Codes, building codes, health regulations, and safety standards. Understanding of plumbing-related mechanical equipment including pumps, water heaters, pressure-reducing stations, expansion systems, and water treatment components. Familiarity with blueprint reading, schematics, specifications, and construction documents. Perform other tasks assigned by the manager in response to the needs of the university. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Connecticut P-2 or P-1 Plumbing License required. High school diploma or GED required; completion of an accredited HVAC technical school program, trade school certificate, or equivalent vocational training preferred. Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible plumbing experience in commercial, institutional, healthcare, higher education, or industrial facilities. Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Backflow Prevention Certification. OSHA 10 or OSHA 30 certification. Knowledge of steam, hydronic, and mechanical building systems. Experience supporting renovation and construction projects. Ability to install, repair, maintain, and test plumbing systems and components. Skilled in diagnosing system failures and determining effective corrective actions. Proficient in pipe fitting, soldering, brazing, threading, welding coordination, and fixture installation. Ability to perform inspections and compliance testing of plumbing systems. Competence in operating plumbing equipment, drain-cleaning machines, pipe threading equipment, leak detection devices, and testing instruments. Unusual Working Conditions Works in a variety of indoor and outdoor environments under varying weather conditions, including extreme heat, cold, rain, snow, and humidity. Regularly works in confined spaces, crawl spaces, tunnels, utility vaults, mechanical rooms, construction areas, and other restricted-access locations. May be exposed to wastewater, sewage systems, domestic water systems, chemical treatment equipment, dust, dirt, odors, noise, vibration, and potentially unsanitary conditions. May be exposed to cleaning agents, solvents, adhesives, fluxes, fuels, and other chemicals associated with plumbing and maintenance operations. Performs physically demanding work requiring prolonged standing and walking; climbing ladders, scaffolding, lifts, and stairs; and frequent bending, kneeling, crouching, reaching, and working in awkward positions. Regularly lifts, carries, pushes, and pulls tools, equipment, materials, and piping components weighing up to 50 pounds independently, with assistance or mechanical lifting devices used for heavier items. May work around energized mechanical equipment, pressurized piping, natural gas systems, hot water systems, and steam-related infrastructure. Required to wear appropriate Personal Protective Equipment (PPE), including safety glasses, gloves, hearing protection, protective footwear, respirators, and other safety equipment as required. Must be available to respond to emergency service calls and participate in an on-call rotation, which may include evenings, weekends, holidays, severe weather events, and other emergency campus operations. May be required to perform or support planned utility shutdowns outside normal business hours to minimize disruption to University operations. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. In accordance with Connecticut General Statutes § 31-51v, applicants selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment drug test as a condition of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of both the background check and drug test. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $39.82 - $49.75 per hour Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Hourly Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
