    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7890": {
      "title": "Radiography - Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Radiography - Adjunct Instructor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Radiography - Adjunct Instructor Req #233 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University’s College of Health Professions invites applications for part-time adjunct faculty to support the Associate of Science in Radiography program as instructional needs arise. The Radiography program prepares students for entry-level practice in the medical imaging field through a curriculum that combines foundational sciences, radiologic sciences, and patient care. Coursework includes areas such as image production and acquisition, equipment operation, quality control, radiation protection, digital imaging, and specialized imaging modalities. Responsibilities: Teach assigned didactic courses in on-ground and/or online formats. Develop and facilitate instructional content and assess student learning. Use a variety of instructional strategies to engage students and support learning outcomes. Utilize Blackboard Ultra to manage course materials and communication. Provide regular and timely feedback to students and be available for student support. Advise students on matters related to academics, clinical progress, attendance, and professional expectations. Maintain and report grades and attendance in accordance with University policies. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree preferred. Current ARRT® certification and registration in Radiography (R); additional credentials in Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance (MR), and/or Mammography (M) are preferred. Current State of Connecticut Radiographer license. Minimum of two years of professional experience. Prior college-level teaching experience and proficiency with an online course management system are preferred. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit a letter of interest, current CV, statement of teaching philosophy, and relevant examples from courses taught (if applicable). Upon offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to provide one formal letter of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting their highest earned degree. Please apply online via this portal. Faxes and emails will not be accepted. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $4,300–$5,400 per 3-credit course. Adjunct Instructors are not eligible to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, they are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan . Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
