cognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here The Jack Welch College of Business & Technology invites applications for the position of Adjunct Instructor in the Department of Management .  The department offers a variety of programs and courses with multiple degree options: Undergraduate Bachelor of Science in Management Minor in Business Minor in Business Law Minor in Management Minor in Sales Management Minor in Global Business Management Minor in Innovation & Entrepreneurship Minor in Human Resource Management Minor in Supply Chain Management Dual Degree Program Bachelor’s-Master of Business Administration (MBA) 4+1 Dual Degree Program Graduate Master of Business Administration (MBA) Graduate Certificate in Human Resource Management Graduate Certificate in Leadership Graduate Certificate in Artificial Intelligence Requirements: A minimum of a master's degree in a closely related field is required and prior higher education level instruction experience will be preferred. The successful candidate will actively promote a collegial environment and consciously apply our mission and values to create a safe space where all may thrive and succeed. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit a letter of interest, current CV, statement of teaching philosophy, and relevant examples from taught courses (if applicable). Please provide one letter of recommendation or accurate contact information. Official transcripts will be required upon offer of employment. Our review of applications will be ongoing based on the needs of the department. Thank you for your interest in Sacred Heart University. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $4,300–$5,400 per 3-credit course. Adjunct Instructors are not eligible to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, they are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan . Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Master’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, Connecticut, United States of America ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
