    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7686": {
      "title": "Club Sports Powerlifting Head Coach",
      "description": "Club Sports Powerlifting Head Coach | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Club Sports Powerlifting Head Coach Req #901 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary The Sacred Heart University Department of Club Sports and Recreation is seeking a Head Coach for its Club Powerlifting team. The Head Coach will be responsible for the recruitment and retention of players, practice preparation, instructional coaching, and other administrative duties for the team.  This part-time position will run from September 1 through May 15 of each academic year. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Responsible for the recruitment of prospective students who will meet University admission standards. Responsible for all league-required paperwork, as well as understanding all rules associated. Foster and enhance relationships with other coaches. Responsible for the retention of all team members, particularly first-year students, and ensuring their transition into college is seamless. Work with the Club Sports staff to develop a cohesive program and highlight it via social media and the Club Sports website. Develop a recruitment plan beyond the upcoming season. Create and implement a weekly practice plan to ensure all team members are prepared for competition. The coach should demonstrate strong leadership, communication, and organizational abilities. Prepare, plan, and coordinate practice schedules each week and provide proper and high-end instruction to student-athletes. Work with the Athletic Training staff on player safety and development. Oversee all game day responsibilities, including game planning, transportation, and game roster. Work closely with the Club Sports and Recreation department on the preparation of the season, schedule, and recruitment. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor’s degree preferred Minimum of 3 years of coaching experience at the high school, prep, junior, or collegiate level. Possess experience working with diverse staff, including college-age students. Must maintain coaching certification or be willing to acquire certification. CPR/First Aid Certification Unusual Working Conditions Night and weekend availability is required. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The salary range for this position is $2,500 - $3,000 Non-benefit eligible employees are unable to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, part-time, non-benefit eligible employees are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, but they are not eligible to receive the employer matching contributions, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Temporary, per-diem, and seasonal staff are not eligible to participate in the 403(b) retirement plan. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Employment Indicator Part-time Seasonal Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/7679": {
      "title": "Chemistry - Adjunct Instructor (On-Going)",
      "description": "Chemistry - Adjunct Instructor (On-Going) | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Chemistry - Adjunct Instructor (On-Going) Req #162 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University’s Department of Chemistry in the College of Arts and Sciences invites applications for adjunct faculty positions to teach introductory undergraduate courses and labs in various areas of chemistry:  General Chemistry lab, Organic Chemistry lab, Chemistry for nurses lectures and labs. Graduate-level a djuncts are also needed to teach courses in Analytical Chemistry, Chromatography and Spectroscopy. Candidates must have a Ph.D. or Master’s degree in Chemistry and prior teaching experience. Graduate-level instructors must have a Ph.D. in Chemistry and practical experience within this field. The successful candidate will actively promote a collegial environment and consciously apply our mission and values to create a safe space where all may thrive and succeed. Applicants should submit C.V., cover letter and contact information for one personal reference via this online portal. Official transcript(s) and one letter of recommendation will be required upon formal offer of employment. Questions regarding this position may be addressed to Dr. Linda Farber, Department Chair. Applications will be reviewed as they are received and qualified candidates will be considered until our needs are met. Online submissions only, please Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $4,300–$5,400 per 3-credit course. Adjunct Instructors are not eligible to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, they are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan . Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
